11hf|n|Remedy; relief; amends; reparation; hence, one who brings relief. ; That which is given to make an exchange equal, or to make up for the deficiency of value in one of the things exchanged. ; Profit; gain; advantage; use. ; A covering for the foot and lower part of the leg, ordinarily made of leather. ; An instrument of torture for the leg, formerly used to extort confessions, particularly in Scotland. ; A place at the side of a coach, where attendants rode; also, a low outside place before and behind the body of the coach. ; A place for baggage at either end of an old-fashioned stagecoach. ; An apron or cover (of leather or rubber cloth) for the driving seat of a vehicle, to protect from rain and mud. ; The metal casing and flange fitted about a pipe where it passes through a roof. ; Booty; spoil.	a:3wqq,102,18;hf7,94,13;5b2v,90,12;2okx,88,36472;9r0w,86,16;4hy3,83,4;abqs,81,540;77c5,76,209;tgs,74,15;7kl4,73,456;9qy5,73,31;77qw,72,339;43uc,70,15;akqg,68,48;4803,68,2~2okx,88,36472;8ewu,59,6632;3b5p,5,4216;36dg,38,2694;1n86,55,2264;6azn,13,1786;6eqb,19,1645;8800,34,1518;5b9n,28,1509;9ycs,14,1336;1993,4,1305;8rvd,29,1193;5a7n,19,1034;7h25,16,833;7eau,18,747	v:7kl4,64,233;9iy1,63,3;5e7b,61,2;2pbr,54,8;8yfw,52,4567;8xm2,48,2;1ecr,43,3;7x1v,36,3;3gq0,32,4;77c5,31,9;7x2h,30,35;6dst,28,25;43je,27,19;3c4c,25,18;7x1m,24,4~8yfw,52,4567;1etz,9,621;8fmf,5,347;8ewu,15,294;36dg,3,238;7kl4,64,233;4dyf,1,154;4dqq,13,87;ab0x,9,78;alrg,5,77;1tr9,17,73;9vm0,11,66;3vqs,3,60;1n86,1,57;7dth,4,45	V:948e,69,75;ahii,67,2;ak7v,67,3;18tw,59,16;18s3,47,262;2j8a,40,7;8hhq,37,48;yut,37,2;6x60,37,2;52xn,37,4;2v65,37,1772;948b,35,12;1h2k,35,7;2gzp,35,1104;42zf,31,4~akfc,18,2754;2v65,37,1772;2gzp,35,1104;9wql,15,344;35j3,0,292;5q3c,1,278;1pvn,18,272;18s3,47,262;35ku,2,189;5bwc,16,92;8ohy,15,78;948e,69,75;5e6y,5,50;1tr2,5,50;8hhq,37,48	n:4a6p,104,50;7kl4,93,1803;7u4r,89,1577;9r0w,87,17;9ym5,86,7531;aubs,85,23;tgs,83,27;9yns,82,9;2s05,81,4360;30sa,81,21;4bkd,76,4;8ewu,75,18912;43ue,74,6;4my0,73,